# Keep host dependencies and build outputs out of Linux image builds.
#
# Every Dockerfile installs and builds inside the image, so none of these belong in a build context.
# They matter most in the e2e job (.github/workflows/e2e.yml), which builds the stack from a
# checkout the host has just installed and built: without this file each `COPY <package-dir>` would
# carry that host state, never match the layer cache docker.yml writes from a clean checkout on
# main, and rebuild every image from that layer down.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.DS_Store

# Local env files can hold secrets: deployer private keys, RPC keys, wallet-api tokens. A Dockerfile
# that copies a package directory whole would carry them into the image, and a Vite build would read
# `.env.production.local` into the public bundle. CI builds from a clean checkout, but an image built
# on a developer's machine would not be. The committed `.env.example` templates hold no secrets.
# `services/custom-example/.env.development` is excluded too: it serves `pnpm dev` only.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
